#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
Necklace Soliton Dynamics via the 2D Gross-Pitaevskii Equation
==============================================================
REFACTORED VERSION: Computation and visualization are fully decoupled.

All simulation data (including full energy/norm/Lz time series) are
persisted to JSON.  All eight figures can be regenerated from JSON +
snapshot files alone, without rerunning the solver.

Architecture
------------
  Phase 1 — Computation  : run_*() functions  → JSON + .npy snapshots
  Phase 2 — Visualization: fig_*() functions  ← JSON + .npy snapshots only

JSON files written
------------------
  single_ring.json       ← Fig 1, Fig 3, Fig 4 (panel a)
  collision_k1p5.json    ← Fig 2, Fig 3
  scan1d.json            ← Fig 4 (panel b)
  convergence.json       ← Fig 5
  scan2d.json            ← Fig 6
  collision_scan.json    ← Fig 7, Fig 8

JSON schema (common fields)
---------------------------
Every simulation JSON contains at least:
  {
    "meta": {
      "label":       str,       # human-readable run identifier
      "git_hash":    str|null,  # reproducibility
      "device":      str,
      "timestamp":   str,       # ISO-8601
      "corrections": [str]      # physics corrections applied
    },
    "config": { ... },          # full SimConfig as dict
    "validation": { ... },      # output of cfg.validate()
    "timeseries": {             # one entry per saved snapshot
      "t":       [float],
      "E":       [float],       # total energy (H_rot when Omega != 0)
      "E_kin":   [float],
      "E_int":   [float],
      "E_trap":  [float],
      "N":       [float],
      "Lz":      [float],
      "rho_max": [float],
      "E_err":   [float],       # |ΔE/E0|
      "N_err":   [float],       # |ΔN/N0|
      "Lz_err":  [float]        # |ΔLz|
    },
    "summary": {
      "E0":          float,
      "N0":          float,
      "Lz0":         float,
      "rho0_max":    float,
      "max_E_err":   float,
      "max_N_err":   float,
      "max_Lz_err":  float,
      "rho_ratio":   float,
      "collapsed":   bool,
      "Lz_abs_min":  float,
      "Lz_abs_max":  float
    },
    "snap_files": [str],        # ordered list of .npy paths
    "snap_dir":   str
  }

Physical model
--------------
  i ∂_t ψ = [−½∇² + V_trap(r) + g|ψ|²] ψ
  V_trap(r) = ½ V_trap r²  (isotropic harmonic, g < 0 attractive)

Time integration: BAB Strang symmetric split-step pseudo-spectral,
second-order accurate in dt.

Physics corrections [C1]–[C10] are identical to the previous version.

Authors : [Author names]
Journal : [Target journal]
Date    : 2025
"""

